data sources  : the manifest record lists no API data source, but the web page IS data-bound — it reads
                useTirePressure (GET /tire-pressure/latest?vehicle_id={id}) + useTirePressureHistory
                (GET /tire-pressure?vehicle_id={id}), both already exposed by the shared S8 VehicleSystemsStore.
                So the port binds those two feeds (+ SettingsStore unit/locale + the app-scoped
                SelectedVehicleStore) through a ViewModel exposing StateFlow<UiState>. The view performs NO HTTP
                (ADR-002/ADR-004). The four corner pressures are SI Pascals on the wire; conversion to the
                user's display unit (bar/psi) happens ONLY at the render boundary via the shared
                convertPressureFromSI, exactly like the web convertPressureFromSI(pa/1000, unit)
                (unit-conversion.instructions / frontend-si-cutover).
  - useTirePressure         GET /tire-pressure/latest?vehicle_id={id} -> VehicleSystemsStore.tirePressure(id)
                            seam: TirePressurePageSource.tirePressureLatest (TirePressurePageSource.kt L31)
  - useTirePressureHistory  GET /tire-pressure?vehicle_id={id}        -> VehicleSystemsStore.tirePressureHistory(id)
                            seam: TirePressurePageSource.tirePressureHistory (TirePressurePageSource.kt L34)

