================================================================================

panel map    : the 9 manifest panels = 3 web <GlassPanel> usages named in the manifest (GlassPanel1 warning banner
               L407, GlassPanel2 current-readings L430, GlassPanel3 per-corner gauge cell L448) + 4 web <MetricCard>
               tiles (Avg-Pressure / Min-Pressure / Warning-Count / Last-Updated) + 2 web <GlassPanel> usages
               (GlassPanel8 history chart L514, GlassPanel9 history table L565). All 4 MetricCards always render
               (em-dash / 0 before data) and every panel always shows -> no hidden sections (ADR-011 #6). The optional
               web AITirePressureTrendReasoning narrator is conditionally null (withAiFeature) and never a
               deterministic panel, so it is not a parity unit (out of scope, as the sibling VampireDrain narrator).
charts       : 2 native chart wrappers, never a webview — 4x RadialGauge (Compose canvas), one per corner, swept to the
               display pressure and colored by the gauge tier (web pressureColor normal/soft/critical -> theme status
               colors); LineChartWrapper (Vico) plotting the four corner pressures over the history window, values
               converted SI Pa -> the user's display unit at the boundary. The web LINE_COLORS corner->palette mapping
               (fl=0, fr=2, rl=1, rr=3) is reproduced.
states       : the latest feed drives the page loading(PageLoader)/error(ErrorDisplay+retry)/success(panels); the
               history feed drives the chart's own ChartStatus.Loading/Empty and the table's EmptyState/loading. So
               loading/empty/error/success are all implemented and no region is ever blank (ADR-011). isEmpty={false}
               keeps zero/empty snapshots as content so the panels always render with internal empty surfaces (web
               parity — the web never replaces the deterministic panels with a page-level empty state). The inline
               error banner (web AlertBanner) surfaces error.loadFailed when the history feed fails while the latest
               reading still renders.
units        : the four corner pressures are SI Pascals on the wire + through the cache; display conversion to bar/psi
               happens only at the render boundary via the shared convertPressureFromSI (web convertPressureFromSI(
               pa/1000, unit)). The interim raw->Pa coercion (web normaliseTpmsToPa, for vehicles missing a unit-history
               row) is ported verbatim. Nothing is stored/computed non-SI (frontend-si-cutover / unit-conversion.instructions).
i18n         : every visible literal via stringResource (ADR-014); web key names kept. The shared keys reuse the
               generated res/values catalog (translation_tirePressure_title/_subtitle, translation_Time/Warnings/Ok,
               translation_error_loadFailed + the loader/retry/freshness/error-title chrome strings); the literal-key
               labels (web i18next-fallback-only, absent from the generated catalog) live in the app-owned
               res/values/tire_pressure_strings.xml, English-only so ar/he fall back to values/ — reproducing the web's
               missing-key fallback in every locale (vampire_drain_strings precedent). The per-corner TIRE_LABELS +
               STATUS_LABELS (plain English literals in the web source) are also resourced so the surface carries zero
               hardcoded text.
a11y         : Compose semantics paneTitle for the screen title (tirePressure.title); accessibleDescription on the
               history chart + the RadialGauge component descriptions; the VehicleSelect aria label (tirePressure.
               selectVehicle) exposed as a contentDescription; the chart's expandable accessible data table is the
               screen-reader fallback for the canvas; >=48dp Material 3 targets; dynamic-color + dark theme via
               MaterialTheme tokens; no hardcoded colors/typography (ADR-005/ADR-015).
nav          : Destinations 'tirePressure' -> /tire-pressure pre-existing (Destinations.kt L104, count unchanged); host
               wired via PageHosts.register("tirePressure") in TeslaSyncApplication.onCreate; deep links auto-registered
               by the NavHost. DataContainer gains vehicleSystemsStore (the shared S8 VehicleSystemsStore was present in
               apps/shared/core but not yet wired into the Android container; added mirroring energyStore so the surface
               binds an S8 holder per ADR-004, not the network).
